content.details:
CONFIGURATION: Federation is declared in config.json under the federation key. Each namespace maps a name to a kb_path (relative to the main KB's path), a description, and a search_default flag.

Example:
{
  "federation": {
    "namespaces": {
      "auth": {"kb_path": "../team-auth-kb", "description": "Auth team KB", "search_default": true},
      "infra": {"kb_path": "../team-infra-kb", "description": "Infra KB", "search_default": false}
    }
  }
}

RESOURCES: Each namespace gets scoped resources — knowledge://auth/index, knowledge://auth/health, knowledge://auth/stats, knowledge://auth/changelog. The main KB is accessible via knowledge://index etc (namespace=default).

TOOLS: All search/load/list/expand/deep_search tools accept an optional namespace parameter. New federated_search tool searches across multiple namespaces and returns results grouped by namespace.

CACHE ISOLATION: ModuleCache keys include namespace prefix (namespace:module_id). Same module ID in different namespaces won't collide in cache.

AUTO-DETECTION: The MCP server auto-detects federation from config.json. No --federation CLI flag needed.
